# Security

- Never commit secrets, `.env`, API keys, or credentials. Use env vars / secret stores.
- Do not build SQL or shell commands by concatenating untrusted input — use parameters / safe APIs.
- Mutations require **server-side** authorization checks (UI checks are not enough).
- Do not log tokens, passwords, session cookies, or unnecessary PII.
- Validate untrusted input at the trust boundary (HTTP body/query, file uploads, webhooks).

```typescript
// BAD
await pool.query(`SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ${req.params.id}`);

// GOOD
await pool.execute('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [req.params.id]);
```
